# Forever Profession Guides — Project Rules

## 1. Strict WoW: Forever Only Scope
- Target **World of Warcraft: Forever (`1.60.1`, `Interface: 16001`) ONLY**.
- Never use Retail (Dragonflight/TWW/Midnight), Vanilla Classic Era, or Season of Discovery recipes, skill thresholds, or mechanics unless verified against the local Forever reference data (`C:\Users\axolatl-tank\Projects\polestar\data\forever\`).
- Remember Forever-specific mechanics: 600+ new recipes, Scarce bonus materials (`Frilled Lichen`, `Rosecap`, `Stranglevine`, `Pyrite`, `Bauxite`, `Pitchblende`, `Pristine Leather/Hide/Scale`), Alchemy dyes & Sulfuric Acid, Engineering Sandpaper, First Aid healing potions, Camping features (skill 20+), Well Fed +5% kill XP, and Legacy Points at 150/225/300 for the 6 crafting professions only.

## 2. Never Guess IDs or Coordinates
- Look up every quest, NPC, object, item, spell, inn, flight point, and guide ID via `polestar find <query> --json` before writing it.
- Keep `pack.json` at the repo root and `.guide` files under `guides/`. Never commit compiled `.lua` or `.toc` files (except `locales/<locale>/*.lua` generated by `forge i18n guides sync`).

## 3. Multi-Profession Leveling Rules
Follow `docs/MULTI_PROFESSION_RULES.md`:
- **Per-File Structure (No Monoliths):** Each single profession gets its own `.guide` file at `guides/<profession>.guide` (`forever-professions/<profession>`), and each paired profession combination gets its own separate `.guide` file at `guides/pairs/<partner>-<anchor>.guide` (`forever-professions/pair-<partner>-<anchor>`, `folder Paired Routes`). Never combine multiple solo professions or multiple combinations into one giant guide file.
- **Single-Anchor Sections:** `forge guide lint` requires all `section <Profession> <from>-<to>` headers in one `.guide` file to belong to ONE profession in rising order. Anchor `section` on the crafting (or producer) profession and interleave partner `train`, `skill`, `collect ... gather`, and `craft` steps inside each section.
- **Materials Symmetry:** Every `collect ... gather` inside a section MUST have a matching `auction <item> xN` in the same section so Mix/Gather/Buy modes work cleanly. Never put `auction` on a BoP item.

## 4. External Data Sources & Verification Gate
- Reference online databases (Wowhead, Questie, QuestDB/QuestieDB, Forever client tables, etc.) for factual WoW: Forever game data so every guide is verified, working, and maximally optimized for Forever (`1.60.1`).
- Always preserve all licenses and attributions of external data sources.
- Before finishing any guide edit, run from this folder until both pass with **0 errors and 0 warnings**:
```powershell
forge guide lint --format json
polestar playtest
```
For guides using `when skill`, also test with `polestar playtest --learn "<ProfA>,<ProfB>"`.
